{"body":"Independent adversarial review of the approved #914 replacement found raw CultureMech term IDs promoting labels with no MIM name owner into unrelated or insufficiently scoped MIM identities.\n\nConfirmed cases:\n- `MnSO4·xH2O` becomes anhydrous CHEBI:86360/CAS7785-87-7 (17 occurrences), despite existing MIM rejection of variable-hydrate aliases. Source: CultureMech `bacterial/JCM_J1503_AUTOTROPHIC_NITROBACTER_MEDIUM.yaml`; [ChEBI86360](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:86360) denotes the anhydrous salt.\n- `Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12)` becomes generic class CHEBI:176843 through `algae/yt75s_v.yaml`, despite the MIM class record explicitly rejecting the cyanocobalamin member name. [ChEBI176843](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:176843) is the class.\n\nTen additional preparation-qualified labels have no MIM name anchor and acquire pure-compound identity through the same fallback:\n- `1 M K2HPO4` → `CHEBI:131527`\n- `1 M KH2PO4` → `CHEBI:63036`\n- `1 M Sodium acetate solution` → `CHEBI:32954`\n- `1 M Tris base (pH 8)` → `CHEBI:9754`\n- `1 N NaOH` → `CHEBI:32145`\n- `10% Glucose solution` → `CHEBI:17234`\n- `25% HCl (7.7 M)` → `CHEBI:17883`\n- `5% L-Cysteine·HCl·H2O solution` → `CHEBI:91248`\n- `5% Na2S·9H2O solution` → `CHEBI:76209`\n- `8% NaHCO3 solution` → `CHEBI:32139`\n\nUnder MAPPING_SEMANTICS §0 these need explicit preparation-scope review, not inferred exact identity. The safe export repair rejects the named raw source ID for that exact label without inventing a replacement or minting a record. The existing four-column rejection ledger currently cannot express a rejection without an asserted replacement MIM ID; its supported contract must be extended narrowly in the producer and local gate. Keep source names/counts, scope rejections by label+ID, preserve a valid explicit MIM name owner, and do not globally blacklist an ontology term. Regenerate with zero unsafe identities on these held pairs, add regressions, rerun native QC and independent review.\n\nThis is a dependency of the approved #914 redo, separate from step5 SSSOM owned-name policy. Existing related source/label issues #811 and #868 remain distinct. Evidence: `output/approved-plan-20261101T031134Z/step1-independent/unified-fallback-findings.json` and `unified-54-identity-owner-check.json`; diagnostic snapshot SHA256 `e5c4bd6b5512606857feded03a45591476ce64626c261315f7ed2bed1f742f8a`. No scientific approval is granted by withholding.\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABhpWP9Q","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"The required Step 1 review expanded the bounded cohort from the original 12 examples to **33 exact label/source-ID pairs**. Both the author and independent reviewer ran the actual current `_anchor_record` resolver with the current MIM indexes and live records: all 33 have no independent owner. The decision is to withhold each listed source pair without inventing a replacement, under MAPPING_SEMANTICS section 0. This is a unified source-fallback repair; it does not advance the later SSSOM alias-policy step.\n\n| Source label | Rejected source ID | Source evidence at CultureMech `a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c` |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 M K2HPO4 | CHEBI:131527 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/archaea/TOGO_M1265_Modified_Cellulolytic_Haloarchaea_Medium.yaml) `$.solutions[3].composition[0]` |\n| 1 M KH2PO4 | CHEBI:63036 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/archaea/TOGO_M1265_Modified_Cellulolytic_Haloarchaea_Medium.yaml) `$.solutions[3].composition[1]` |\n| 1 M Sodium acetate solution | CHEBI:32954 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/TOGO_M873_Syfac_Medium.yaml) `$.solutions[2]` |\n| 1 M Tris base (pH 8) | CHEBI:9754 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/archaea/TOGO_M970_Peat_Medium_2_For_Methanobacteria.yaml) `$.solutions[2].composition[0]` |\n| 1 N NaOH | CHEBI:32145 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/brucella_blood_agar_with_hemin_menadione.yaml) `$.solutions[0].composition[1]` |\n| 10% Glucose solution | CHEBI:17234 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/mediadive_4784_Main_sol_J825.yaml) `$.composition[12]` |\n| 25% HCl (7.7 M) | CHEBI:17883 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/archaea/JCM_J1427_MODIFIED_METHANOBACTERIUM_MEDIUM.yaml) `$.solutions[0].composition[0]` |\n| 5% L-Cysteine·HCl·H2O solution | CHEBI:91248 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/archaea/JCM_J1422_METHANOCORPUSCULUM_AGGREGANS_MEDIUM.yaml) `$.ingredients[12]` |\n| 5% Na2S·9H2O solution | CHEBI:76209 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/archaea/JCM_J1422_METHANOCORPUSCULUM_AGGREGANS_MEDIUM.yaml) `$.ingredients[13]` |\n| 8% NaHCO3 solution | CHEBI:32139 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/archaea/JCM_J1422_METHANOCORPUSCULUM_AGGREGANS_MEDIUM.yaml) `$.ingredients[11]` |\n| Cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12) | CHEBI:176843 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/algae/yt75s_v.yaml) `$.solutions[0].composition[0]` |\n| MnSO4·xH2O | CHEBI:86360 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/JCM_J1503_AUTOTROPHIC_NITROBACTER_MEDIUM.yaml) `$.solutions[1].composition[0]` |\n| 1 M CaCl2 solution | CHEBI:3312 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/archaea/TOGO_M1265_Modified_Cellulolytic_Haloarchaea_Medium.yaml) `$.solutions[0].composition[4]` |\n| 1 M K2HPO4 solution | CHEBI:131527 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/TOGO_M1220_Natronospira_Proteinivora_Medium.yaml) `$.solutions[0].composition[4]` |\n| 1 M MgCl2 solution | CHEBI:6636 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/archaea/TOGO_M1150_Natranaeroarchaeum_Medium.yaml) `$.solutions[1].composition[8]` |\n| 1 M Sodium fumarate solution | CHEBI:115156 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/TOGO_M873_Syfac_Medium.yaml) `$.solutions[3]` |\n| 1 N KOH | CHEBI:32035 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/algae/wees.yaml) `$.solutions[5].composition[2]` |\n| 2 M NH4Cl solution | CHEBI:31206 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/TOGO_M1220_Natronospira_Proteinivora_Medium.yaml) `$.solutions[1].composition[5]` |\n| 3% L-Cysteine HCl x H2O solution | CHEBI:91248 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/mediadive_4784_Main_sol_J825.yaml) `$.composition[14]` |\n| 3% Na2S x 9 H2O solution | CHEBI:76209 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/mediadive_4784_Main_sol_J825.yaml) `$.composition[15]` |\n| 4 M NH4Cl solution | CHEBI:31206 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/archaea/TOGO_M1150_Natranaeroarchaeum_Medium.yaml) `$.solutions[1].composition[5]` |\n| 5% Na2S x 9 H2O solution | CHEBI:76209 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/TOGO_M873_Syfac_Medium.yaml) `$.solutions[5]` |\n| Ethanol (95 %) | CHEBI:16236 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/treponema_rectale_medium.yaml) `$.solutions[0].solutions[3].composition[1]` |\n| FeSO4 x 7 H2O (0.1% w/v in 0.1 N H2SO4) | CHEBI:75836 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/archaea/methanofollis_medium.yaml) `$.ingredients[6]` |\n| HEPES buffer pH 7.8 | CHEBI:42334 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/algae/P49_Medium.yaml) `$.solutions[1].composition[1]` |\n| KOH solution | CHEBI:32035 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/archaea/methanobacterium_medium_ii_with_formae.yaml) `$.solutions[0].composition[12]` |\n| NaOH (1 N) | CHEBI:32145 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/taiyang_medium_no_9_prototype.yaml) `$.solutions[1].composition[1]` |\n| Sulfuric acid (concentrated) | CHEBI:26836 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/Bold_Trace_Stock.yaml) `$.composition[0]` |\n| Tricine (pH 8) | CHEBI:46760 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/DAS_Vitamin_Cocktail.yaml) `$.composition[0]` |\n| MnSO4 x xH2O | CHEBI:86360 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/freshwater_thiosulfate_oxidizing_bacteria_medium.yaml) `$.solutions[1].composition[2]` |\n| MnSO4.xH2O | CHEBI:86360 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/TOGO_M332_PE_Medium_pH_7.2.yaml) `$.solutions[3].composition[0]` |\n| Cyanocobalamin (B12) | CHEBI:176843 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/rs_medium_nutrient_medium_nm_component.yaml) `$.solutions[2].solutions[2].composition[0]` |\n| Vitamin B12 (Cobalamin) | CHEBI:176843 | [source](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureMech/blob/a74dd489720c9df96cc073ffd11568d407d3c06c/data/normalized_yaml/bacterial/DAS_Vitamin_Cocktail.yaml) `$.composition[3]` |\n\nHashes, selectors, full contexts and independent anchor checks will be committed with the replacement PR evidence. The four-column ledger will distinguish an explicitly blank replacement (this exact source-label hold) from the existing nonempty corrected identity. An unrelated label sharing the source ID remains unaffected; a future independently curated owner remains authoritative.\n\nProducer dependency: CultureBotAI/culturebotai-claw#697. Consumer: CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech#1025.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-01T03:32:57Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1025#issuecomment-6552915957","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":1025,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Hold unsupported raw-source identity promotions in the refreshed unified snapshot","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1025"}
